# Databricks bundle

`databricks.yml` targets: `dev` (development, default) and `prod`.

Defaults if omitted: catalog `hvacpulse_dev`, schema `streaming`.
The Azure runbook instead passes `--var "schema=hvacpulse"`. Pass the schema
you intend; do not assume the default matches that runbook.

Required vars: `eventhubs_bootstrap` (`<namespace>.servicebus.windows.net:9093`),
`eventhubs_connection_secret` (`hvacpulse:eventhubs-connection`), and
`alert_email` for job failure and duration notifications.
Pipeline conf `hvacpulse.topic` is `hvac.telemetry`. The Event Hub resource
name is `hvac-telemetry`.

```powershell
databricks bundle deploy -t dev --var "eventhubs_bootstrap=<ns>.servicebus.windows.net:9093" --var "eventhubs_connection_secret=hvacpulse:eventhubs-connection" --var "catalog=<catalog>" --var "schema=streaming"
databricks bundle run -t dev hvacpulse_batch
```

Lakeflow owns only `bronze_telemetry`, with `pipelines.reset.allowed=false`;
do not add a dataset that needs a Bronze reset. Silver/quarantine (`run_silver.py`)
and plant (`run_plant.py`) run as job tasks with `availableNow` and checkpoints
on `/Volumes/<catalog>/<schema>/checkpoints`.

Job `hvacpulse_batch`: `max_concurrent_runs: 1`, cron `0 */5 * * * ?` UTC.
Notebooks pass `run_id: "{{job.run_id}}"`. Job `hvacpulse_health` runs every
10 minutes and fails when `pipeline_health` finds a critical stage.
Notebooks are thin wrappers. New shared modules must be listed under
`sync.include`. Cloud plant control stays in shadow mode. Secrets stay in the
Databricks secret scope.
Runbook: `docs/runbooks/azure-databricks.md`.
